# H1 red proof — 1a/06 denies "failed to reproduce"/"could not get it to fail"
# and requires an observed-outcome signal per marker paragraph
# Date: 2026-10-13 (UTC), branch stage-1a-spike, cycle-2 rework follow-up.
# Finding: docs/evidence/1a/qa/cycle2b-r1-recheck.log (commit 3fc5605) —
# the R1 deny list still counted "failed to reproduce" and "could not get
# it to fail" as observations; enumeration alone cannot close the class.
#
# Two mechanisms: (a) DENIAL_RE extended with fail(ed|s|ing) to reproduce,
# could not get ... fail, did(n't) manage, no <token> could be
# produced|reproduced|observed|obtained, nothing (was) produced|...;
# (b) every marker surviving the deny filter must have an observed-outcome
# signal (SIGNAL_RE) in its paragraph (marker line through the next blank
# line). All scratch states restored with `git checkout --` (q03.log is
# committed); q10.log never written.

